WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:04.730
Troubleshooting anything involves a process,
and with networking, it is no different.

00:00:04.730 --> 00:00:08.929
As this course is geared toward networking
for small to medium-sized businesses, there

00:00:08.929 --> 00:00:12.820
are some steps we as network administrators
should use when troubleshooting a networking

00:00:12.820 --> 00:00:14.090
situation.

00:00:14.090 --> 00:00:17.130
Troubleshooting is basically a seven-step
process.

00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:18.730
Step one is to identify the problem.

00:00:18.730 --> 00:00:24.800
In this, we probably need to ask open-ended
questions to try to figure out why, for example,

00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:27.040
a network connection is not working.

00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:29.240
Is the problem isolated to one user?

00:00:29.240 --> 00:00:30.240
Is an entire building affected?

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:35.230
A problem cannot be solved unless we know
what the problem is.

00:00:35.230 --> 00:00:39.630
Step two: Establish a theory of probable cause;
this is a fancy way of saying, let's find

00:00:39.630 --> 00:00:41.410
out what caused the problem.

00:00:41.410 --> 00:00:43.180
Did something get unplugged?

00:00:43.180 --> 00:00:44.900
Is there a misconfiguration?

00:00:44.900 --> 00:00:48.600
Was a rogue device added to the network to
cause a network attack?

00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:50.120
Step three: Test the theory.

00:00:50.120 --> 00:00:51.780
Can we duplicate the problem?

00:00:51.780 --> 00:00:55.410
If we can, it might make it easier to find
a solution.

00:00:55.410 --> 00:00:58.370
Step four is to establish a plan to solve
the problem.

00:00:58.370 --> 00:00:59.600
Is this an easy fix?

00:00:59.600 --> 00:01:03.980
Are we going to need to reboot a server or
do something else that will disrupt services

00:01:03.980 --> 00:01:05.590
temporarily?

00:01:05.590 --> 00:01:09.909
To solve a problem, we need to have an idea
as to how to solve it.

00:01:09.909 --> 00:01:13.159
Step five is to implement the solution or
escalate it as necessary.

00:01:13.159 --> 00:01:17.819
Here, we need to understand a very important
point: If you are the one trying to solve

00:01:17.819 --> 00:01:22.680
a problem and get stuck as to how to it, escalate
it.

00:01:22.680 --> 00:01:28.310
Most network problems are very time-sensitive,
and taking too much time to fix something

00:01:28.310 --> 00:01:34.189
when someone else can do it faster can cause
major problems in timing, data loss, lost

00:01:34.189 --> 00:01:37.249
revenue, and frustrated employees.

00:01:37.249 --> 00:01:40.840
Step six is to verify that the solution worked.

00:01:40.840 --> 00:01:45.709
Before declaring to a customer that a problem
is solved, test out the solution.

00:01:45.709 --> 00:01:48.920
Make sure that the original problem cannot
be replicated.

00:01:48.920 --> 00:01:52.600
Lastly, step seven: Document the solution.

00:01:52.600 --> 00:01:57.310
Many companies use some kind of help desk
ticketing software, SharePoint site, or even

00:01:57.310 --> 00:02:00.259
a database to track problems and solutions.

00:02:00.259 --> 00:02:04.959
Make sure a solution is detailed enough so
that someone else, should they encounter the

00:02:04.959 --> 00:02:07.589
same problem, has an idea of what to do.

